.TH ALBDF 1 "2026-08-05" "albdf 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
albdf \- work with PDF documents via command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B albdf
[\fIoptions\fR] \fIcommand\fR [\fIarguments\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B albdf
is the command-line interface of the albdf headless PDF editing library
(a fork of PDF4QT). It can inspect, render, edit, and manipulate PDF
documents without a GUI. It ships with RTL (Arabic/Persian/Hebrew) text
writing and search support - features not present in upstream PDF4QT.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-console-format <format>
Console output format: \fBtext\fR (default), \fBxml\fR, or \fBhtml\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-text-codec <codec>
Codec for redirected output: \fButf8\fR (default), \fBlatin1\fR, \fBsystem\fR.
Use UTF-8 for XML output.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show command-line help.
.TP
.B \-\-help-all
Show help including generic Qt options.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Show version information.
.SH COMMANDS
Run
.B albdf help
for the full list. This page documents the albdf-specific commands in
detail; the inherited PDF4QT commands (render, fetch-text, info, unite,
separate, redact, encrypt, decrypt, optimize, xml, statistics, ...) keep
their upstream behavior.
.SS add-text
Add a text label to a page.
.PP
.B albdf add-text
.I in.pdf out.pdf
.B \-\-page
.I N
.B \-\-x
.I X
.B \-\-y
.I Y
.B \-\-text
.I "STRING"
.RB [ \-\-size
.IR SIZE ]
.RB [ \-\-rtl
.RB [ \-\-font
.I FONT.TTF
.RB " \-\-lang " fa | ar | he | ur ]]
.TP
.B \-\-page
Page number (1-based).
.TP
.B \-\-x, \-\-y
Baseline position in PDF points (origin bottom-left of the page).
.TP
.B \-\-text
Text to add. For \fB\-\-rtl\fR this is the LOGICAL string (as typed).
.TP
.B \-\-size
Font size in points (default 12).
.TP
.B \-\-rtl
Use the RTL pipeline: FriBidi directional runs, HarfBuzz shaping, and a
fully embedded Type0/Identity-H TrueType font with ToUnicode CMap and
/ActualText marked content. Requires \fB\-\-font\fR and \fB\-\-lang\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-font
TTF font file for RTL text (e.g. Vazirmatn, Noto Naskh Arabic, Noto Sans
Hebrew — all OFL-licensed).
.TP
.B \-\-lang
Language tag: \fBfa\fR, \fB ar\fR, \fBhe\fR, \fBur\fR. Selects script and
bidi base direction.
.SS recognize-text
Recognize page content objects (text, image, path) and print them with
bounding boxes. The printed index is the address space used by
\fBdelete-object\fR.
.PP
.B albdf recognize-text
.I in.pdf
.SS delete-object
Delete a whole content object from a page.
.PP
.B albdf delete-object
.I in.pdf out.pdf
.B \-\-page
.I N
.B \-\-index
.I K
.RB [ \-\-list ]
.TP
.B \-\-page
Page number (1-based).
.TP
.B \-\-index
0-based object index on the page (see \fBrecognize-text\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-list
List objects on the page and exit without modifying anything.
.SS search-text
Search for text in the document, RTL-aware, reporting bounding rectangles.
.PP
.B albdf search-text
.I in.pdf
.I "QUERY"
.RB [ \-\-page\-first
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-page\-last
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-case\-sensitive ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-normalize ]
.TP
.I QUERY
The text to find, in LOGICAL order (as a human would type it).
.TP
.B \-\-page\-first, \-\-page\-last
Page range (1-based; default: all pages).
.TP
.B \-\-case\-sensitive
Match case exactly (default: case-insensitive).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-normalize
Disable RTL normalization. Default normalization: NFKC folding of Arabic
presentation forms and the lam-alef ligature, stripping of tashkeel and
ZWNJ/ZWJ, Persian<->Arabic letter unification (e.g. yeh, keheh, alef
variants, teh marbuta), and Persian/Arabic-Indic digit unification
(so \fB123\fR matches \fB۱۲۳\fR).
.PP
PDF content streams store text in VISUAL order; the engine inverts the
logical query to visual order (FriBidi) before matching, then maps matched
characters back to their bounding rects. Output: a table of page, item,
bounding box (x y w h, PDF points), and matched text.
.PP
A phrase split across two adjacent text-flow items (e.g. after re-flowing
an RTL add on a dense page) is matched as one occurrence; the Item column
then shows the span range, e.g. \fB2+3\fR covers items 2 and 3. Matches
never span lines or columns.
.SS form-list
List interactive form (AcroForm) fields.
.PP
.B albdf form-list
.I in.pdf
.TP
Prints one row per field: name, type (text / button / choice /
signature), current value, page, and widget rectangle. Walks the
AcroForm tree; read-only fields are flagged.
.SS form-fill
Set form field values and write a new document.
.PP
.B albdf form-fill
.I in.pdf out.pdf
.B \\-\\-field
.I name
.B \\-\\-value
.I VALUE
.RB [ \\-\\-field
.I name
.B \\-\\-value
.I VALUE ... ]
.TP
.B \\-\\-field, \\-\\-value
Repeated pairs set field values (text/button/choice). Appearance
streams are regenerated and the result is written to
.I out.pdf.
.SS sign
Apply a PKCS#7 detached digital signature (PAdES-style byte-range).
.PP
.B albdf sign
.I in.pdf signed.pdf
.B \\-\\-cert
.I cert.p12
.B \\-\\-password
.I SECRET
.RB [ \\-\\-reason
.IR REASON ]
.RB [ \\-\\-page
.IR N
.B \\-\\-rect-x
.IR X
.B \\-\\-rect-y
.IR Y
.B \\-\\-rect-w
.IR W
.B \\-\\-rect-h
.IR H ]
.TP
.B \\-\\-cert
PKCS#12 certificate file. Without \\fB\\-\\-page\\fR the signature is
invisible; with a page and rect a visible signature widget is placed.
.TP
.B \\-\\-password
PKCS#12 password.
.TP
.B \\-\\-reason
Optional human-readable signing reason.
.SS verify-signatures
Validate digital signatures in a document.
.PP
.B albdf verify-signatures
.I signed.pdf
.TP
Reports each signature's validity; any tampering of the signed bytes
shows as an error.
.SH RTL BEHAVIOR
.PP
RTL text added with \fBadd-text \-\-rtl\fR extracts in visual order via
\fBfetch-text\fR (PDF stores glyphs visually); full logical fidelity is
carried in the /ActualText marked content. Known limitations:
.TP
\(bu
ToUnicode CMap destinations are limited to one UTF-16 code unit, so
ligatures (e.g. lam-alef) degrade to their first letter in extraction.
Search still finds them thanks to normalization.
.TP
\(bu
Decomposed marks (e.g. Arabic yeh with dots) duplicate their base letter
in extraction.
.TP
\(bu
Vertical mark offsets (diacritic positioning above the base) are dropped
in v1 rendering; glyphs render at the baseline.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 7
Invalid arguments.
Other non-zero codes indicate document read/write or processing errors.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Add a Persian label and search for it:
.PP
.nf
albdf add-text in.pdf out.pdf --page 1 --x 72 --y 700 \\
       --text "سلام دنیا" --size 24 --rtl \\
       --font /usr/share/fonts/truetype/vazirmatn/Vazirmatn-Regular.ttf --lang fa
albdf search-text out.pdf "سلام"
.fi
.PP
Delete the second object on page 1:
.PP
.nf
albdf recognize-text in.pdf
albdf delete-object in.pdf out.pdf --page 1 --index 1
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qpdf (1),
.BR pdftotext (1)
.SH AUTHOR
albdf project — a fork of PDF4QT (MIT) by Jakub Melka and contributors.
